  "scope_note": "Separate per-pane zero-based audition stream selection is preserved by Source preparation, absolute seek, EOF and ready-cache heartbeat, and remains independent of replacement policy. Native selection, admission validation and cache identity prevent a stream-zero result being reused for stream one. A tiny two-second Matroska has mono 440 Hz audio ordinal zero and stereo 880 Hz ordinal one; generated native proxies were decoded and measured under bounded CPU-only diagnostic units. Existing Windows browser verifies default zero, selecting B stream one, unchanged selection/cache through synchronized absolute seek, explicit replacement policy independence and swap reset. Project/history and saved/source hashes are preserved. No browser installation, hardware GPU, native desktop GUI changes or physical audio qualification. Sustained long playback, physical speakers/microphone and frozen/compound replacement remain separate acceptance.",
